Requirements:


1) Book a ride

2) Onboard a driver

3) Driver accepts the ride

4) User Make a payment

5) History of user's rides


Functional Requirements

	Book a ride
	Maintaining a user profile
	Maintaining driver profiles
	Cancel the ride

	Put on waitlist (Peak hours)

Non Functional Requirements

	Read heavy system. (Eventual Consistency)
	Low Latency
	Highly available
	Fault tolerant. (Resilency)

High level

	User --> AppServer --> DB (Us1 , Ride1 , D1) (Cache)


1) POST /v1/app/onboard/driver  ------> more meaningful /v1/app/driver/onboard
		Params : username,location
				licence

2) GET /v1/app/getAvailableRides
		Params: location
		Returns : {Available driver ids}

3) GET /v1/app/driverStatus/id {Async batch process will maintain and update the status of a driver in db}

		Param: driverid
		Returns: OFFLINE/AVAILABLE to take ride

4) POST /v1/app/book/ride.  ------> more meaningful /v1/app/ride/create

		Params: userid,location{lat,long},authtoken (To prevent DOS)
		Return: rideid

5) POST /v1/app/rideid/cancel

		Params:rideid, authtoken


		User --> LoadBalancer(Req Q) --> 1) DriverOnboardingService
										 2) RideBookingService
										 3) UserRegistration

Velachery {D4,D5} (Redis)-> Cache the proximal drivers at most frequently requested location.
										 /v1/app/book/ride -> RideBookingService -->
										 a)ProximityService (Returns the closest drivers)
										 b) Fetch driver info and availabilty from db
										 c) PaymentService (PayPal, UPI)
										 d) All successful payments, Create a ride id (user_id, driver_id, ride_id, rideStatus = INPROGRESS)
										 	driverStatus = BUSY

										 e) Once user completes the ride
										 		driver_status = AVAILABLE
										 		ride_status = COMPLETED.

